  "step_by_step_reasoning": "The visual architecture shows user requests passing through External Data to an Application Load Balancer, which forwards traffic to a Pricing Engine running on Amazon ECS. The Pricing Engine stores the payload in ElastiCache (Redis Payload) and pushes jobs to ElastiCache Task Queues. CPU and GPU Pricing Workers (ECS) monitor the Task Queues, move jobs to Processing Queues, retrieve/compute payloads from Redis Payload, and save results back. A Pub/Sub channel in Redis notifies the Pricing Engine upon completion.",
